# Enforce LF for .mjs test/verify scripts to avoid CRLF/LF SHA discrepancies
*.mjs text eol=lf

# task-72: bash scripts MUST stay LF. CRLF makes them unrunnable.
*.sh text eol=lf

# task-140: lock *.js to LF as well.
#   Why: R5-class judges hash the WORKTREE bytes (sha256), so a CRLF checkout made
#   them fail on Windows while passing on Linux -- a platform-dependent false red.
#   Index side was already clean (42/42 i/lf, 0 committed blobs contain CR);
#   the pollution existed only in the worktree (18/42 w/crlf on Windows).
#   NOTE: never use `* text=auto` here -- all 55 images/cards/*.png contain 0x0D
#   and would be corrupted. Enumerate extensions explicitly instead.
*.js text eol=lf
